# RTOS Quick Reference Card

## Core Initialization
```c
rtos_init();                    // Initialize RTOS
rtos_start();                   // Start scheduler
```

## Task Management
```c
// Create task (priority: 0=highest, 511=lowest)
task_tcb_t* task = rtos_task_create(func, "name", priority, arg);

rtos_task_delay(ticks);         // Delay current task
rtos_task_yield();              // Yield to another task
rtos_task_suspend(task);        // Suspend task
rtos_task_resume(task);         // Resume task
rtos_task_delete(task);         // Delete task
task_tcb_t* t = rtos_task_get_current(); // Get current task
```

## Semaphores
```c
semaphore_t* sem = rtos_semaphore_create(initial_count);
rtos_semaphore_wait(sem, timeout);    // Wait (decrement)
rtos_semaphore_signal(sem);           // Signal (increment)
rtos_semaphore_delete(sem);           // Delete
```

## Mutexes (with Priority Inheritance)
```c
mutex_t* mtx = rtos_mutex_create();
rtos_mutex_lock(mtx, timeout);        // Lock (blocks if owned)
rtos_mutex_unlock(mtx);               // Unlock
rtos_mutex_delete(mtx);               // Delete
```

## Message Queues
```c
message_queue_t* q = rtos_queue_create(size);
rtos_queue_send(q, msg, timeout);     // Send message
rtos_queue_receive(q, &msg, timeout); // Receive message
rtos_queue_delete(q);                 // Delete queue
```

## Timers
```c
timer_t* tmr = rtos_timer_create(period_ms, callback, arg, periodic);
rtos_timer_start(tmr);                // Start timer
rtos_timer_stop(tmr);                 // Stop timer
rtos_timer_delete(tmr);               // Delete timer
```

## Interrupts
```c
rtos_interrupt_register(irq_num, handler, priority);
rtos_interrupt_enable(irq_num);       // Enable IRQ
rtos_interrupt_disable(irq_num);      // Disable IRQ

rtos_critical_enter();                // Disable interrupts
// Critical code here
rtos_critical_exit();                 // Enable interrupts
```

## Constants
```c
UINT32_MAX         // Infinite timeout
0                  // No wait (non-blocking)
RTOS_OK            // Success
RTOS_ERROR         // General error
RTOS_TIMEOUT       // Operation timed out
RTOS_WOULD_BLOCK   // Would block (non-blocking call)
```

## Common Patterns

### Producer-Consumer (Semaphore)
```c
semaphore_t *sem = rtos_semaphore_create(0);

void producer(void *arg) {
    while(1) {
        produce_data();
        rtos_semaphore_signal(sem);  // Signal consumer
    }
}

void consumer(void *arg) {
    while(1) {
        rtos_semaphore_wait(sem, UINT32_MAX);  // Wait for data
        consume_data();
    }
}
```

### Shared Resource Protection (Mutex)
```c
mutex_t *resource_mtx = rtos_mutex_create();

void task_a(void *arg) {
    rtos_mutex_lock(resource_mtx, UINT32_MAX);
    // Access shared resource
    rtos_mutex_unlock(resource_mtx);
}
```

### Message Passing
```c
message_queue_t *q = rtos_queue_create(10);

// Sender
void sender(void *arg) {
    int *msg = malloc(sizeof(int));
    *msg = 42;
    rtos_queue_send(q, msg, UINT32_MAX);
}

// Receiver
void receiver(void *arg) {
    void *msg;
    rtos_queue_receive(q, &msg, UINT32_MAX);
    int value = *(int*)msg;
    free(msg);
}
```

### Periodic Timer
```c
void timer_cb(void *arg) {
    // Called every period
}

timer_t *tmr = rtos_timer_create(100, timer_cb, NULL, true);
rtos_timer_start(tmr);
```

## Priority Guidelines
- **0-99**: Critical real-time tasks (interrupts, control loops)
- **100-299**: Normal priority tasks (data processing, communication)
- **300-510**: Background tasks (logging, housekeeping)
- **511**: Idle task (automatic, do not use)

## Memory Usage
- Each task: ~4KB (1KB stack + TCB)
- Semaphore: 32 bytes
- Mutex: 32 bytes
- Queue: 32 bytes + buffer
- Timer: 32 bytes

## Best Practices
1. Always check return values
2. Use timeouts to prevent deadlocks
3. Keep critical sections short
4. Match every create with a delete
5. Don't call blocking functions from ISRs
6. Acquire mutexes in consistent order